  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Grace. Your identity is verified, and I've pulled up order K-9201 from Green Bowl, delivered on October 24 at 6:40 PM.\n\nI can see both items on the order: one Grain bowl ($18.00) and Lemonade ($4.00 each, you ordered two). Since you mentioned one lemonade, I'll treat that as one missing. Your order had a FALL15 promo, so the refund amounts are reduced by each item's share of the discount.\n\nYou have two options for each missing item:\n\n**Option A: Refund to your Visa ending 4242**\n- Grain bowl: $13.50\n- Lemonade: $3.00\n- Total: $16.50\n\n**Option B: Account credit (item price plus 20%)**\n- Grain bowl: $21.60\n- Lemonade: $4.80\n- Total: $26.40\n\nAccount credit is capped at $25 per conversation, so I can't give both items as credit. I could give the grain bowl as credit ($21.60) and refund the lemonade to your card ($3.00). Or I can refund both to your card ($16.50).\n\nWhich would you prefer?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, the split sounds good to me: grain bowl as account credit and the lemonade back on my card. Thanks for working that out."
  },
